melody:
# Verse 1
By yon bon-nie banks and by yon bon-nie braes,
D4/ F#4/ G4 G4/ ~A4/ B4 A4/ G4/ A4 A4/ G4/ E4
where the sun shines bright on Loch Lo-mond,
D4/ F#4/ G4 G4 G4 B4/ D5/ E5(2) D5.
where me and my true love were ev-er wont to gae,
D5/ E5 E5/ D5/ B4 B4/ D5/ C5/ B4/ A4/ G4/ E4
on the bon-nie, bon-nie banks o' Loch Lo-mond.
D4/ F#4/ G4/ G4/ B4/ D5/ E5 D5/ B4/ A4(2) G4

# Chorus
O ye'll tak' the high road and I'll tak' the low road, and
D4 G4 G4/. A4// B4 B4/. A4// G4 G4/. E4// D4 D4/. F#4//
I'll be in Scot-land a-fore ye;
G4 G4/ G4/ G4 B4/ D5/ E5(2) D5.
but me and my true love will ne-ver meet a-gain,
D5/ E5 E5/ D5/ B4 B4/ D5/ C5/ B4/ A4/ G4/ E4
on the bon-nie, bon-nie banks o' Loch Lo-mond.
D4/ F#4/ G4/ G4/ B4/ D5/ E5 D5/ B4/ A4(2) G4(2)
